Egypt to Lebo-hamath, to bring the ark of God from Kiriath-jearim.","verse":5},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"David","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":34,"href":"?bref=1Chr.13.1-16.43","rawReference":"1Chr.13.1-16.43"}],"ruleId":"David::David::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"David"},"text":"David and all Israel went up to Baalah of Judah (that is, Kiriath-jearim) to bring up from there the ark of God the LORD, who is enthroned between the cherubim—the ark that is called by the Name.","verse":6},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"David","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":34,"href":"?bref=1Chr.13.1-16.43","rawReference":"1Chr.13.1-16.43"}],"ruleId":"David::David::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"David"},"text":"David and all the Israelites were celebrating before God with all their might, with songs and on harps and lyres, with tambourines, cymbals, and trumpets.","verse":8},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"David","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":34,"href":"?bref=1Chr.13.1-16.43","rawReference":"1Chr.13.1-16.43"}],"ruleId":"David::David::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"David"},"text":"Then David became angry because the LORD had burst forth against Uzzah. So he named that place Perez-uzzah, as it is called to this day.","verse":11},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"David","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":34,"href":"?bref=1Chr.13.1-16.43","rawReference":"1Chr.13.1-16.43"}],"ruleId":"David::David::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"David"},"text":"That day David feared God and asked, “How can I ever bring the ark of God to me?”","verse":12},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"David","senseEvidence":{"basis":"